b/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341465/field-2/8ec194ddd369d933f19adb1373346bc1deb09c766eb6cb64c74a6206a7328cea" :answer/id #uuid "f74b45a3-64b0-5dd8-b50f-a611882d3ae4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s>5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341465/field-2/93c41a3c94ec1e83d0dcad30c77e97ac14062957975ad4fb34260262061598b6" :answer/id #uuid "c2ae94e4-29ba-599a-b2dc-d0533db01296" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s\\ge 5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341465/field-2/9aa9dfbc88f5063553a847c368b29cb8dda581610b843fa8c8f6be915eb97944" :answer/id #uuid "c9fad298-2b55-57f1-adbc-517c91c39c2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341465/field-2/de63348529d477cd70740ab9581d04b231678372657a4ecc21dd12e21b5d033c" :answer/id #uuid "cba23107-83bc-5ed0-9a4a-0d0d97bd7d7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341465/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "98b28611-7ed9-537e-a6d8-23bb4fbe9332" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-341465/field-2/de63348529d477cd70740ab9581d04b231678372657a4ecc21dd12e21b5d033c" :answer-field/choices ["q-341465/field-2/ccd37af225235e99e0c0beacf5c114a7061b025eb104267b602d298657c10927" "q-341465/field-2/9d34e85dabb5082358af9360d93c7ce717fcea0db3670310b8eab46db4fc35b5" "q-341465/field-2/8ec194ddd369d933f19adb1373346bc1deb09c766eb6cb64c74a6206a7328cea" "q-341465/field-2/93c41a3c94ec1e83d0dcad30c77e97ac14062957975ad4fb34260262061598b6" "q-341465/field-2/9aa9dfbc88f5063553a847c368b29cb8dda581610b843fa8c8f6be915eb97944" "q-341465/field-2/de63348529d477cd70740ab9581d04b231678372657a4ecc21dd12e21b5d033c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341465" :question/id #uuid "8cf6501c-88d1-5bcb-ba50-40bbf2b67514" :question/math-academy-id "q-341465" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t},\\, & t\\le 1 \\\\ 1\\, & t>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t},\\, & t\\le 1 \\\\ 1\\, & t>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{5t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{5t-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{(5-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{(5-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5-s}{[{e}^{(5-s)t}]}_{0}^{1}+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{-{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-as}-{e}^{-s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{-s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}+\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341465/field-1" "q-341465/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "424fc261-d1ca-5bf0-b085-7af1de6cc7cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341465"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341464/field-1/