d "e5b3901e-c1c6-5348-864d-60f3574ecd1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-341464" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t},\\, & t\\le 2 \\\\ 2\\, & t>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t},\\, & t\\le 2 \\\\ 2\\, & t>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{3t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{3t-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-s}{[{e}^{(3-s)t}]}_{0}^{2}+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{-2{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-as}-{e}^{-2s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{-2s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341464/field-1" "q-341464/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/val